 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Acrylic dries with a layer of water on top of the paint, which can make it look flatter. A quick fix is to spray a thin layer of lacquer over the painting while it' still wet. Yes, tape a small area with a tester paint and let it dry. If it looks dull, lacquer it. If it stays bright, leave it as is. add a gloss varnish with a glitter or a metallic powder. Sprinkle the powder evenly over wet paint and let it dry.",
